147 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(A caesarean birth is not a failure, a shortcut, or \215the easy way out.\216 It is major surgery, yes, but it is also a powerful, valid way to bring your baby into the world and a deeply personal birth experience. For some families, a caesarean is planned in advance; for others, it becomes the safest choice during labour or pregnancy. Many parents feel a mix of emotions, relief, grief, excitement, or disappointment , and all of these are normal and valid.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

148 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(What matters most is not how your baby arrives, but that you feel informed, respected, and supported throughout.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

149 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(Caesareans happen for many reasons: baby\220s position, placenta concerns, multiples, previous caesarean, maternal health, or sometimes personal choice. Some are planned calmly; others happen more urgently. Both are real births and both deserve preparation. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

150 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(Not all caesareans are the same, some are planned, some unplanned, some urgent, and some can even be \215gentle caesareans,\216 where the birth is slowed and personalised to support connection and bonding.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

151 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(A caesarean is major surgery and carries risks: longer recovery, more pain, risk of infection or bleeding, and potential impact on future pregnancies. It can also affect you emotionally, especially if the birth feels out of your control. Knowing this does not create fear, it gives you the power to make informed choices and prepare fully.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

152 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(Even in surgery, you have rights, you have the right to clear information, consent before procedures, respectful communication, a partner present where safe, and choices about atmosphere, bonding, and feeding. Skin to skin, early feeding, and emotional support are all possible, and your voice still matters.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

153 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(Planning a caesarean is not about controlling everything. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

154 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 89 0 R/E(It is about understanding your options, clarifying what matters to you, and creating a sense of agency in a situation that can otherwise feel overwhelming. When you plan, you move from \215this is happening to me\216 to \215I am part of this.\216 You are not just a patient, you are a birthing parent, and your caesarean birth deserves just as much intention, respect, and tenderness as any other birth.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

155 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 89 0 R/T(why caesarean?)/E(why caesarean?)/Pg 11 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

156 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 90 0 R/T(A caesarean is major surgery, and like any operation, it carries risks. But knowing these risks helps you make informed choices, feel prepared, and advocate for your care. Most caesareans \204 whether planned or emergency \204 result in healthy parents and babies, especially when the surgery is well-managed and supported.)/E(A caesarean is major surgery, and like any operation, it carries risks. But knowing these risks helps you make informed choices, feel prepared, and advocate for your care. Most caesareans \204 whether planned or emergency \204 result in healthy parents and babies, especially when the surgery is well-managed and supported.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

157 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 90 0 R/T(Maternal Risks)/E(Maternal Risks)/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

158 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 863 0 R/T(Even in a planned caesarean, there are some risks to be aware of:)/E(Even in a planned caesarean, there are some risks to be aware of:)/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

159 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 864 0 R/T(Wound or uterine infection: slightly higher after emergency procedures.)/E(Wound or uterine infection: slightly higher after emergency procedures.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

160 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 865 0 R/T(Excessive bleeding: sometimes requiring a blood transfusion.)/E(Excessive bleeding: sometimes requiring a blood transfusion.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

161 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 866 0 R/T(Blood clots: slightly increased risk compared with vaginal birth.)/E(Blood clots: slightly increased risk compared with vaginal birth.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

162 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 867 0 R/T(Damage to nearby organs: such as the bladder or ureters \(rare\).)/E(Damage to nearby organs: such as the bladder or ureters \(rare\).)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

163 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 868 0 R/T(Longer recovery: caesareans usually take several weeks to fully heal.)/E(Longer recovery: caesareans usually take several weeks to fully heal.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

164 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 869 0 R/T(Impact on future pregnancies: slightly higher risk of uterine rupture \(~1 in 500\), placenta previa, or placenta accreta \(~1 in 1,000\) compared with parents who have only had vaginal births.)/E(Impact on future pregnancies: slightly higher risk of uterine rupture \(~1 in 500\), placenta previa, or placenta accreta \(~1 in 1,000\) compared with parents who have only had vaginal births.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

165 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 870 0 R/T(Emergency caesareans carry higher maternal complication rates than planned ones, including infection, blood loss, and longer hospital stays.)/E(Emergency caesareans carry higher maternal complication rates than planned ones, including infection, blood loss, and longer hospital stays.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

166 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 90 0 R/T(Neonatal \(Baby\) Risks)/E(Neonatal \(Baby\) Risks)/Pg 12 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

167 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 871 0 R/T(Babies born via caesarean are generally healthy, but there are some differences compared with vaginal birth:)/E(Babies born via caesarean are generally healthy, but there are some differences compared with vaginal birth:)/Pg 12 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

168 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 872 0 R/T(Breathing or respiratory difficulties: more common if the baby is born before labour or before 39 weeks.)/E(Breathing or respiratory difficulties: more common if the baby is born before labour or before 39 weeks.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

169 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 873 0 R/T(Emergency C-sections: up to 18% of babies experience mild respiratory issues.)/E(Emergency C-sections: up to 18% of babies experience mild respiratory issues.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

170 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 874 0 R/T(Elective C-sections at term: around 5%.)/E(Elective C-sections at term: around 5%.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

171 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 875 0 R/T(Neonatal intensive care \(NICU\) admission: slightly higher after emergency caesareans.)/E(Neonatal intensive care \(NICU\) admission: slightly higher after emergency caesareans.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

172 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 876 0 R/T(Lower Apgar scores at birth: occasionally reported in emergency situations.)/E(Lower Apgar scores at birth: occasionally reported in emergency situations.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

173 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 877 0 R/T(Planning your caesarean around 39 weeks can help reduce some of these risks.)/E(Planning your caesarean around 39 weeks can help reduce some of these risks.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

174 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 90 0 R/E(These numbers show relative risk, but most caesareans result in healthy outcomes, especially when planned and medically supervised.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

175 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 90 0 R/T(caesarean birth: understanding the risks)/E(caesarean birth: understanding the risks)/Pg 12 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

176 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 91 0 R/T(WHY THESE NUMBERS MATTER,  BUT DON\220T DEFINE YOUR BIRTH)/E(WHY THESE NUMBERS MATTER,  BUT DON\220T DEFINE YOUR BIRTH)/Pg 13 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

177 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Knowledge is power. Understanding risks allows you to prepare physically and emotionally.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

178 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Most complications are rare, and most babies do very well after caesarean birth.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

179 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Emergency caesareans naturally carry higher risks because they are performed due to complications \204 the risks are not caused by the surgery itself.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

180 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Being informed means you can plan for comfort, bonding, and emotional connection, making your birth positive and empowering, even in surgery.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

181 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(Bottom Line)/Pg 13 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

182 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(A caesarean is a safe and valid way to give birth. Being aware of risks allows you to make choices that protect you and your baby, while still reclaiming this as your birth. With preparation, planning, and support, you can experience a calm, connected, and empowering caesarean birth, every bit as meaningful as any other way of welcoming your baby.)/Pg 13 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

183 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 91 0 R/E(How does this make you feel?)/Pg 13 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

184 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(The chances are you know what hypnobirthing is at this point. Let\220s sum it up below just to be sure and to help explain to partners, family or friends who may think it\220s a load of rubbish!)/Pg 14 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

185 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(So here it is!)/Pg 14 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

186 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(It\220s getting informed about birth- It\220s learning all about the process of birth, the hormones involved, how to choose your birth place, how your environment can help you to feel positive and help the process along, the role of the birth partner, the stages of labour, positions to help aid baby\220s position, how to write a birth plan and all sorts of other stuff that if you haven\220t been at loads of births \(and most of us haven\220t\) you just won\220t know unless you\220ve been told it or sought it out. The more you know about birth, the more likely it is that you will feel prepared )/Pg 14 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

187 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(to face it yourself.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

188 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(It\220s a change of mindset- Knowing what the body is doing and HOW can really help you to see birth as a positive thing and take a lot of the fear away. Between getting as informed as possible and taking in lots of positive information about birth, you can completely change your mindset from one full of fear of what can \217go wrong\220 into one that expects birth to \217go right\220 \(whatever that means\). Feeling positive and confident at the start of labour can go a long way to helping the process along by keeping away from fight or flight and producing lots of oxytocin.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

189 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(It\220s learning decision making tools- Knowing your rights when it comes to birth \(psst, you can pretty much do what you want\) and knowing how and where to get all the information you need, helps you to feel informed and confident in making the decisions needed to birth your baby. This may be during pregnancy, by getting information from third parties such as AIMS  or doing your own research. It may be during labour, in which case using decision making tools designed to get as much information about your circumstances will help you to make decisions about your care. Just knowing the questions to ask to find out if it\220s safe to take 30 mins to make your decision can make a huge difference. Nobody wants to make a decision in a rush when some time could have been taken to process it and ensure the choices were understood and considered and the best one for the family chosen!)/Pg 14 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

190 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(It\220s the hypnobirthing tools you\220ve probably heard about- Last but not least there are the famous hypnobirthing tools, what comes to mind when people say hypnobirthing \(aside from swinging clocks and vagina whispering\). These tools are an incredible way to prepare for birth and remain calm and comfortable throughout. However, on their own without all the stuff above, they\220re not enough. Add these into your routine alongside all the information and mindset stuff and you have got this!)/Pg 14 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

191 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(Breathing Techniques- These ensure you\220re taking lots of nice big even breaths throughout your labour to keep the oxygen flowing nicely, this will help your uterus to be able to do it\220s job as efficiently and comfortably as possible. They are also a great way of distracting you from what\220s going on around you and giving you something else to focus on. )/Pg 14 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

192 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(It sounds simple but breathing techniques can do so much to keep you calm and if )/Pg 14 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

193 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 92 0 R/E(you practice them during pregnancy you will feel the benefit on the day.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

194 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 92 0 R/T(wtf is hypnobirthing?)/E(wtf is hypnobirthing?)/Pg 14 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

195 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(Visualisation- This is a way to almost practise birth before its time to do it for real. Thinking in your head about how you\220d like your birth to go or saying it out loud, can help you to feel more confident in your plans and trick your mind into thinking it\220s nothing new when labour starts for real! This can help reduce the chance of entering fight or flight and keep oxytocin flowing!)/E(Visualisation- This is a way to almost practise birth before its time to do it for real. Thinking in your head about how you\220d like your birth to go or saying it out loud, can help you to feel more confident in your plans and trick your mind into thinking it\220s nothing new when labour starts for real! This can help reduce the chance of entering fight or flight and keep oxytocin flowing!)/Pg 15 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

196 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(Affirmations- Using the law of repetition, you can convince your brain to believe something just by showing it the same information repeatedly. Instead of talking about how you DON\220T want labour to go, write affirmations and say things about how you DO want it to go. Giving your brain a bit of cheerleading can help it to believe in you! Instead of saying \217I don\220t want to tear\220 say \217my body WILL stretch to accommodate my baby\220. After a while the affirmations sink into your subconscious and help you to have confidence in yourself which in turn will help )/E(Affirmations- Using the law of repetition, you can convince your brain to believe something just by showing it the same information repeatedly. Instead of talking about how you DON\220T want labour to go, write affirmations and say things about how you DO want it to go. Giving your brain a bit of cheerleading can help it to believe in you! Instead of saying \217I don\220t want to tear\220 say \217my body WILL stretch to accommodate my baby\220. After a while the affirmations sink into your subconscious and help you to have confidence in yourself which in turn will help )/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

197 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(you feel more relaxed and encourage the hormones needed for labour.)/E(you feel more relaxed and encourage the hormones needed for labour.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

198 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(Relaxation- As humans living in a world full of things to do, technology etc. we rarely spend time relaxing and doing absolutely nothing! This means that our neocortex, the part of our brain responsible for rational thinking, is almost never switched off. We very much want that part of the brain to be out of the way during labour and not interfering with the process by thinking of unhelpful scenarios! By practising relaxation during pregnancy, you can make it easier to relax on cue, a skill that\220s very handy for labour! Try lying back and doing absolutely nothing, on the sofa, in bed or in the bath, wherever you like! If you find it difficult to switch )/E(Relaxation- As humans living in a world full of things to do, technology etc. we rarely spend time relaxing and doing absolutely nothing! This means that our neocortex, the part of our brain responsible for rational thinking, is almost never switched off. We very much want that part of the brain to be out of the way during labour and not interfering with the process by thinking of unhelpful scenarios! By practising relaxation during pregnancy, you can make it easier to relax on cue, a skill that\220s very handy for labour! Try lying back and doing absolutely nothing, on the sofa, in bed or in the bath, wherever you like! If you find it difficult to switch )/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

199 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(off then doing something that doesn\220t require much thought counts too! Colouring in, knitting/ crochet, walking in nature etc. may be more your thing. Do what works for you!)/E(off then doing something that doesn\220t require much thought counts too! Colouring in, knitting/ crochet, walking in nature etc. may be more your thing. Do what works for you!)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

200 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(Hypnobirthing tracks- Listening to hypnobirthing tracks will help you to relax, they are usually written by hypnotherapists and therefore help to induce a state of calm and relaxation. The words will also provide you with lots of encouragement and self belief as they talk you through how amazing you and your body are. Don\220t worry if you fall asleep listening to them, they will still be going into your subconscious even if you\220re not actively listening. Just be sure you don\220t listen when driving or operating heavy machinery as this is not safe. It\220s fine to listen to affirmation tracks anytime though for that little boost of confidence!)/E(Hypnobirthing tracks- Listening to hypnobirthing tracks will help you to relax, they are usually written by hypnotherapists and therefore help to induce a state of calm and relaxation. The words will also provide you with lots of encouragement and self belief as they talk you through how amazing you and your body are. Don\220t worry if you fall asleep listening to them, they will still be going into your subconscious even if you\220re not actively listening. Just be sure you don\220t listen when driving or operating heavy machinery as this is not safe. It\220s fine to listen to affirmation tracks anytime though for that little boost of confidence!)/Pg 15 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

201 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(Anchoring- Whilst you are practising relaxation you can help by setting up cues for your brain to associate with relaxation and therefore help you to do it whenever you want, these are called anchors. Anchors can help you to incorporate all 5 senses and therefore make the conditions seem the same wherever you are. You may spray a room spray or have an essential oil that you use whilst relaxing that you then use in labour, you may have a blanket or cushion that you have with you whilst relaxing that you can have with you in your birth space or you may use your hypnobirthing tracks or relaxing music to aid your relaxation, then you can use this during labour and it will all help you to relax despite other things being different such as the location \(or the fact you\220re in labour eeek!\).)/E(Anchoring- Whilst you are practising relaxation you can help by setting up cues for your brain to associate with relaxation and therefore help you to do it whenever you want, these are called anchors. Anchors can help you to incorporate all 5 senses and therefore make the conditions seem the same wherever you are. You may spray a room spray or have an essential oil that you use whilst relaxing that you then use in labour, you may have a blanket or cushion that you have with you whilst relaxing that you can have with you in your birth space or you may use your hypnobirthing tracks or relaxing music to aid your relaxation, then you can use this during labour and it will all help you to relax despite other things being different such as the location \(or the fact you\220re in labour eeek!\).)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

202 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 93 0 R/T(TOP TIP- Use all the hypnobirthing tools at once throughout your pregnancy and in labour and see how chilled you can feel! )/E(TOP TIP- Use all the hypnobirthing tools at once throughout your pregnancy and in labour and see how chilled you can feel! )/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

203 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(Hypnobirthing can be incredibly useful even for a caesarean birth, whether planned or unplanned. Many people assume hypnobirthing is only for natural labour, but its tools are just as effective in surgery \204 for reducing fear, stress, and tension, and for creating a more calm, empowered experience. How?)/Pg 16 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

204 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 94 0 R/T(hypnobirthing for caesarean?)/E(hypnobirthing for caesarean?)/Pg 16 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

205 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(1. Reduces Fear and Anxiety)/Pg 16 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

206 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E( Fear and tension increase pain perception, blood pressure, and stress hormones. Hypnobirthing teaches techniques such as deep breathing, visualisation, and positive affirmations calm your nervous system. Even in a caesarean theatre, these tools help you stay grounded, relaxed, and in control of your emotional state.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

207 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(2. Enhances Focus and Presence)/Pg 16 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

208 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E( Hypnobirthing teaches you to tune inward and focus on the birth you want, rather than feeling swept along by events. In a caesarean, this can help you remain mentally present for meeting your baby, communicating your needs to the surgical team, and noticing those special first moments.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

209 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(3. Supports Relaxed Muscle Tone)/Pg 16 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

210 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(Tension can make anaesthesia less effective and slow recovery. Hypnobirthing techniques like guided visualisations and progressive relaxation help keep muscles soft and relaxed, making the surgery physically easier and more comfortable.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

211 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(4. Prepares Your Mind for the Unexpected)/Pg 16 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

212 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E( ven if your caesarean is planned, surgery can still feel unpredictable. Hypnobirthing encourages mental flexibility: imagining different scenarios, reinforcing positive outcomes, and creating calm responses for surprises. This can reduce fear if things change last minute.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

213 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(5. Improves Bonding and Birth Satisfaction)/Pg 16 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

214 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(A calm, relaxed birth fosters oxytocin release, even in surgery. Using hypnobirthing techniques during your caesarean can enhance your connection with your baby, support skin to skin and early breastfeeding, and help you feel emotionally present rather than detached.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

215 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(6. Empowers You and Your Birth Partner)/Pg 16 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

216 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 94 0 R/E(Hypnobirthing isn\220t just about relaxation; it\220s about knowledge, agency, and teamwork. Your birth partner can learn scripts, breathing techniques, and visualisations to support you, advocate for your preferences, and create a calm, safe environment for both of you.)/Pg 16 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

