endobj

640 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(So much time and energy is spent preparing for birth, yet the days and weeks after birth\204the fourth trimester\204are where families often need the most support. This is a time of profound transition, when your baby is adjusting to life outside the womb and you are adjusting to life as a parent.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

641 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Your newborn\220s needs are simple but intense: closeness, warmth, feeding, and responsive care. Frequent waking, cluster feeding, and a strong desire to be held are not signs of \215bad habits\216\204they are normal, biologically driven behaviours that help your baby feel safe and secure. Planning ahead for these realities can make the early weeks feel less overwhelming and more supported.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

642 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(At the same time, your body and mind are undergoing enormous change. Hormones shift rapidly after birth, which can affect your emotions, energy levels, and sense of identity. Feeling tearful, sensitive, euphoric, anxious, or unsure at times is common\204and you are not alone. Preparing for this emotional landscape, alongside practical needs like meals, rest, feeding support, and household help, can create a softer landing into parenthood.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

643 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Postpartum planning is not about perfection\204it\220s about permission: permission to rest, to ask for help, to move slowly, and to prioritise connection over productivity. By thinking ahead about support, boundaries, and nourishment\204both physical and emotional\204you give yourself and your baby the best possible start in this tender, transformative season.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

644 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Research consistently shows that practical support, emotional validation, and realistic expectations significantly improve parental wellbeing and reduce the risk of postnatal anxiety and depression. Preparing for the fourth trimester is one of the most powerful ways to care for yourself and your baby.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

645 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Key themes:)/Pg 38 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

646 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1043 0 R/E(Talk openly about how life might change after birth.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

647 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1044 0 R/E(Normalise feelings of uncertainty, grief for old routines, or identity shifts.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

648 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1045 0 R/E(Create space for connection, not perfection.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

649 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 116 0 R/E(Becoming a parent is a major psychological transition. Mixed emotions are normal\204even when a baby is deeply wanted and loved.)/Pg 38 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

650 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 117 0 R/T(postnatal expectations/planning)/E(postnatal expectations/planning)/Pg 39 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

651 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(After pains)/Pg 39 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

652 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(The cramps known as afterbirth pains, or simply afterpains, are caused by contractions of your uterus as it returns to its pre-pregnancy size after you have your baby, and expels any clots. \(This process is called "involution."\))/Pg 39 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

653 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(This can intensify when feeding, but is not usually something to be concerned about, and is often more common after subsequent births. Taking paracetemol or ibuprofen is safe and can help.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

654 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Bleeding \(AKA Lochia\))/Pg 39 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

655 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(It usually begins straight after birth and can continue for up to six weeks postpartum; however, the heaviest flow tends to be during the first two weeks. you mnay fins clots, anything bigger than a 50p should be monitored and anything bigger than your palm should be checked. Between around days four and 10, lochia should get lighter and have a more pinkish or brownish hue. This will still happen following a caesarean.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

656 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Never use a tampon!)/Pg 39 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

657 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Swelling )/Pg 39 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

658 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(You may experience some vaginal swelling as well as swelling to your vulva. This is quite common, and usually reduces after 2-3 days.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

659 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Use 'padsickles' \(maternity pad, socaked in aloe and witch hazel and popped int he freezer\) to help, plus arnica to reduce any bruising.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

660 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Other areas may still have access water, but this too should reduce in a couple of weeks!)/Pg 39 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

661 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Stitches)/Pg 39 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

662 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(If you've had stitches after tearing or an episiotomy, keep them clean by bathing daily, to help prevent infection. Use plain warm water then carefully pat yourself dry.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

663 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(If your stitches are sore or uncomfortable, tell your midwife.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

664 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Stitches usually dissolve themselves, but sometimes they have to be taken out- check with your midwife.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

665 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Using a Peribottle \(or just a jug of warm water\) may help reduce any stinging also.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

666 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Baby blues)/Pg 39 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

667 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Are due to a sudden drop of hormones, which your body tries to process over the first few days post birth.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

668 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 117 0 R/E(Symptoms of baby blues include: feeling emotional, irrational or overwhelmed, tearful \(without knowing why\), irritable and moody and down or anxious. They usually pass, but if you find they're sticking around, seek support from your midwife or other agens including PANDAS.)/Pg 39 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

669 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Colostrum)/E(Colostrum)/Pg 40 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

670 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Colostrum is a highly concentrated form of breast milk and is what your breast/chest produces in the first few days after your baby being born. Because it\220s so concentrated, colostrum often has a thick consistency, and a golden yellow colour. )/E(Colostrum is a highly concentrated form of breast milk and is what your breast/chest produces in the first few days after your baby being born. Because it\220s so concentrated, colostrum often has a thick consistency, and a golden yellow colour. )/Pg 40 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

671 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Colostrum contains high levels of fat, protein and carbohydrates, so your baby will be able to get plenty of nutrition even from the small quantities you produce.*liquidgold*)/E(Colostrum contains high levels of fat, protein and carbohydrates, so your baby will be able to get plenty of nutrition even from the small quantities you produce.*liquidgold*)/Pg 40 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

672 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Going to the loo)/E(Going to the loo)/Pg 40 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

673 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(You might be shitting yourself \(excuse the pun\) at the thought of going to the loo post birth.)/E(You might be shitting yourself \(excuse the pun\) at the thought of going to the loo post birth.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

674 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Try not to hold it, your bladder may have lower levels of control, so go as soon as you feel it. Drink lots to dilute the urine too.)/E(Try not to hold it, your bladder may have lower levels of control, so go as soon as you feel it. Drink lots to dilute the urine too.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

675 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(You probably won't have a poo for a few days after the birth, but it's important not to let yourself get constipated. Eat lots of fibre and drink lots of water to help keep your stools soft, occasionally a laxitive may be helpful. \(p.s. its very unliely your stutches will burst\).)/E(You probably won't have a poo for a few days after the birth, but it's important not to let yourself get constipated. Eat lots of fibre and drink lots of water to help keep your stools soft, occasionally a laxitive may be helpful. \(p.s. its very unliely your stutches will burst\).)/Pg 40 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

676 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Piles)/E(Piles)/Pg 40 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

677 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Piles can be quite common \(yes I had them\).)/E(Piles can be quite common \(yes I had them\).)/Pg 40 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

678 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Try not to push or strain when going to the toilet to help prevent and use 'Anusol' or similar to help the discomfort of they happen. They usually go away within a few days. Be aware of your diet to help your stolls stay soft too.)/E(Try not to push or strain when going to the toilet to help prevent and use 'Anusol' or similar to help the discomfort of they happen. They usually go away within a few days. Be aware of your diet to help your stolls stay soft too.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

679 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Night Sweats)/E(Night Sweats)/Pg 40 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

680 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Postpartum sweating and night sweats are very common and normal, and they usually go away after a few weeks. Strategies that can help include drinking plenty of water to prevent dehydration, and taking a lukewarm or cool shower before bed)/E(Postpartum sweating and night sweats are very common and normal, and they usually go away after a few weeks. Strategies that can help include drinking plenty of water to prevent dehydration, and taking a lukewarm or cool shower before bed)/Pg 40 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

681 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/P 118 0 R/T(Any questions or if you want any support, always contact me and I can signpost/support you if necessary.)/E(Any questions or if you want any support, always contact me and I can signpost/support you if necessary.)/Pg 40 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

